# constraint_notnull_only_via_and.tkr — the SM-G12 (crumb 0018) `notnull` guard regression. The
# broadened term grammar now threads `pending_gt` through every constraint atom; `notnull` must
# still be rejected as a `|` alternative (it enters a constraint ONLY via `&`, e.g. `class &
# notnull`) — the one case the self-build/fixpoint never exercises (it never compiles rejected code).

Feature: constraint_notnull_only_via_and — `notnull` stays `&`-only after the term-grammar broadening

  Scenario: notnull_in_or_rejected — `notnull` as a `|` alternative is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "`notnull` may not be a `|` alternative — it is a non-null modifier, use it with `&` (e.g. `class & notnull`) (§9.2b)"
